NNAAMMEE
       setsid - run a program in a new session

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       sseettssiidd [options] _p_r_o_g_r_a_m [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t_s]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       sseettssiidd runs a program in a new session. The command calls ffoorrkk(2) if
       already a process group leader. Otherwise, it executes a program in the
       current process. This default behavior is possible to override by the
       ----ffoorrkk option.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --cc, ----ccttttyy
           Set the controlling terminal to the current one.

       --ff, ----ffoorrkk
           Always create a new process.

       --ww, ----wwaaiitt
           Wait for the execution of the program to end, and return the exit
           status of this program as the exit status of sseettssiidd.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Display version information and exit.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

